Subject: [flux] Name the executable flux.exe

chrome.exe is Chromium's own output name; nothing in the fork had overridden
it, so the product called Flux shipped a binary called chrome.

Six references, and they have to move together or the series has a state
where the browser is renamed and the things that look for it are not:

- chrome/BUILD.gn links the executable to initialexe/chrome.exe and then
  reorder_imports rewrites it out to chrome.exe. Renaming only one of those
  leaves reorder_imports looking for a file that no longer exists, which
  fails at the very last target of the build.
- chrome_constants.cc hardcodes "chrome.exe" as the name the browser uses to
  find its own executable. This one does not fail the build; it fails later
  and quietly, wherever the browser looks itself up by name.
- The installer packs the browser by name in three places: the archive
  action's input list, the chrome.release manifest that says what goes into
  the install directory, and installer::kChromeExe, which is what setup.exe
  launches and renames on update. Miss any of them and the installer builds
  an archive around a file that is not there.

- build/win/reorder-imports.py is the one that actually bit. The GN action
  passes DIRECTORIES, not filenames, so the script itself hardcodes
  chrome.exe on both sides. Renaming the GN inputs/outputs alone changes
  dependency metadata and nothing else: the linker wrote initialexe/flux.exe,
  the script went looking for initialexe/chrome.exe, found the PREVIOUS
  BUILD's copy still sitting there, reprocessed that, and reported success -
  so out/Dev/chrome.exe was a stale binary and out/Dev/flux.exe never existed.
  A GN action's inputs and outputs are a promise to ninja about what the step
  touches; they do not rename anything.

chrome.dll is deliberately NOT renamed. The exe loads it through chrome_elf by
name, and that name reaches into chrome_elf, the version resources and the
crash handler. The DLL is an implementation detail nobody sees; the exe is
what has Flux's icon on it in the task manager.

--- a/chrome/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/BUILD.gn
@@ -87,12 +87,12 @@
     # initialexe/ is used so that the we can reorder imports and write back to
     # the final destination at $root_out_dir/.
     inputs = [
-      "$root_out_dir/initialexe/chrome.exe",
-      "$root_out_dir/initialexe/chrome.exe.pdb",
+      "$root_out_dir/initialexe/flux.exe",
+      "$root_out_dir/initialexe/flux.exe.pdb",
     ]
     outputs = [
-      "$root_out_dir/chrome.exe",
-      "$root_out_dir/chrome.exe.pdb",
+      "$root_out_dir/flux.exe",
+      "$root_out_dir/flux.exe.pdb",
     ]
     args = [
       "-i",
@@ -150,9 +150,9 @@
   }
 
   if (is_win) {
-    _chrome_output_name = "initialexe/chrome"
+    _chrome_output_name = "initialexe/flux"
   } else {
-    _chrome_output_name = "chrome"
+    _chrome_output_name = "flux"
   }
 
   executable("chrome_initial") {

